Exercise: sa-ssh-review (chapter 10 lab)

Work on workstation as student, and on servera as root (ssh root@servera).

Access for an account
 1. An account ops on servera (password Ops-Pass-2026). Log in to it from
    workstation with a key pair you create, ~/.ssh/id_ops, with the public
    key installed through ssh-copy-id. Give it a Host alias opsa in
    ~/.ssh/config.

Hardening (servera)
 2. In /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/10-hardening.conf set:
      PasswordAuthentication no
      X11Forwarding no
      MaxAuthTries 3
      LoginGraceTime 30
    Check with sshd -T, and reload sshd. Do all of it with a second session
    kept open, and test a new key login before you close it.

Files
 3. Copy inventory.txt (from this directory) to the home directory of ops.
 4. Copy the three files in reports/ to /home/ops/mirror/ with rsync
    (rsync -av reports/ opsa:mirror/). Then delete reports/b.txt locally and
    run rsync again with --delete, so b.txt disappears on servera too.

Evidence
 5. Fill in answers.txt: the SHA256 fingerprint of servera's Ed25519 host key
    and the key type.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-ssh-review
